flowchart TB
  accTitle: How a first analysis uses the related repositories
  accDescr: The context step asks GitHub whether each repository of [related] is public; one that isn't, or doesn't exist, is left out with a warning. It searches each public one for the words of the new issue and writes what it finds to related-issues.jsonl, each issue with its repository, and the whole texts to related/. The AI may name those issues as related, never as duplicates, and may say in belongs_in that the issue belongs in one of the related repositories. The apply job links only issues that exist in a public related repository and leaves out the rest, and belongs_in becomes one sentence for the maintainers. Nothing moves or closes on its own: a maintainer transfers the issue by hand.
  config(["[related]<br>repositories"]) --> public{"public?"}
  public -- "no" --> warning["a warning:<br>none of its<br>issues"]
  public -- "yes" --> search["a search for<br>the words of<br>the issue"]
  search --> files[("related-issues.jsonl,<br>related/")]
  files --> ai["`**the AI**<br>related issues<br>with their<br>repository,<br>belongs_in`"]
  ai --> exists{"apply: does<br>the issue exist<br>there?"}
  exists -- "yes" --> link["a link under<br>Related"]
  exists -- "no" --> left["left out"]
  ai --> sentence["one sentence<br>for the<br>maintainers"]
  sentence --> maintainer(["a maintainer<br>transfers it<br>by hand"])
